CAT = "ea3Poa"; SEG = "POA"
# Power of attorney, tax information authorizations and limited representation.
Q = [
("A client wants her bookkeeper to see her IRS account information but not to represent her. She should file:",
 "Form 8821", ["Form 2848", "Form 56", "Form 8822"],
 "Form 8821, Tax Information Authorization, lets a designee inspect or receive confidential tax information without the power to represent. Form 2848 grants representation."),
("Unlike Form 2848, Form 8821 may name as designee:",
 "A corporation", ["Only an attorney", "Only a practitioner", "Only a relative"],
 "Form 8821 authorizes any individual, corporation, firm, organization or partnership to receive information. Form 2848 may name only individuals eligible to practice before the IRS."),
("Line 3 of a client's Form 2848 lists 'Income, 1040, all years.' The IRS will:",
 "Return the form", ["Record every open year", "Record only the current year", "Record it for 3 years"],
 "The Form 2848 instructions say not to use general references such as all years or all taxes, and the IRS returns any power of attorney that does."),
("Future years listed on a Form 2848 are recorded on the CAF only up to:",
 "3 years past the receipt year", ["1 year after the signature date", "The next return's due date", "5 years after the form is signed"],
 "The instructions say the IRS will not record future years or periods that exceed 3 years from December 31 of the year it receives the power of attorney."),
("A representative may sign a client's income tax return under a power of attorney when the client:",
 "Was abroad 60 days before the due date", ["Was abroad 30 days before the due date", "Is too busy to review the return", "Lives in a different state that year"],
 "Regulations section 1.6012-1(a)(5) allows an agent to sign only for disease or injury, continuous absence from the U.S. for at least 60 days before the due date, or with IRS permission for good cause."),
("Spouses who filed jointly want the same EA to represent them. They must:",
 "Each file a separate Form 2848", ["File one Form 2848 together", "Have either spouse sign one form", "Use Form 8821 for the second spouse"],
 "The Form 2848 instructions require spouses who filed a joint return to execute their own separate powers of attorney, even when they authorize the same representative."),
("A client signs Form 2848 first. For a domestic authorization, the representative must sign within:",
 "45 days", ["10 days", "30 days", "60 days"],
 "When the taxpayer signs first, the representative must sign within 45 days of the taxpayer's signature, or 60 days for a taxpayer residing abroad."),
("To revoke a Form 2848 without naming a new representative, the taxpayer:",
 "Marks a copy REVOKE and signs", ["Calls the CAF unit to cancel it", "Files a new Form 8821 instead", "Waits for the years to close"],
 "The instructions say to write REVOKE across the top of the first page, with a current signature and date, and send the copy to the IRS. Without a copy, a signed statement of revocation works."),
("An EA ending representation marks a copy of the power of attorney with which word?",
 "WITHDRAW", ["REVOKE", "RESCIND", "TERMINATE"],
 "A representative withdraws by writing WITHDRAW across the top of the first page with a current signature and date. REVOKE is the taxpayer's annotation."),
("A new Form 2848 for the same tax matter is recorded on the CAF. Unless line 6 says otherwise, the earlier one:",
 "Is generally revoked", ["Stays fully in force", "Lapses after 90 days", "Covers later years only"],
 "A power of attorney recorded on the CAF generally revokes any earlier one recorded for the same matter, unless the taxpayer checks line 6 to retain it."),
("A Centralized Authorization File (CAF) number is:",
 "An IRS-assigned record number", ["Proof of authority to practice", "The EA's enrollment number", "A substitute for the PTIN"],
 "The CAF number is a nine-digit number the IRS assigns to representatives. It is not the SSN, PTIN or enrollment card number and does not show authority to practice."),
("Which matter calls for a specific-use Form 2848 that is not recorded on the CAF?",
 "A private letter ruling request", ["A Form 1040 examination", "A balance due on Form 941", "An installment agreement request"],
 "Line 4 covers one-time or specific matters the IRS does not record on the CAF, such as private letter rulings, EIN applications, Form 843 claims and FOIA requests."),
("Unless line 5a grants the authority, a representative may NOT:",
 "Add another representative", ["Sign a consent to extend the statute", "Inspect the client's tax records", "Agree to proposed audit changes"],
 "A Form 2848 lets the representative sign agreements, consents and waivers by default, but substituting or adding a representative needs written permission or a line 5a grant."),
("Which document may a representative sign only if line 5a language specifically covers it?",
 "Form 907", ["Form 872", "Form 870", "Form 4549"],
 "The instructions say representatives may not sign Form 907, Agreement to Extend the Time to Bring Suit, unless line 5a covers it. Statute extensions and audit agreements are default authority."),
("For the same matter, how many representatives may receive copies of IRS notices?",
 "2", ["1", "3", "4"],
 "The instructions say a taxpayer may not designate more than two representatives on Form 2848 to receive copies of notices and communications for the same matter."),
("An executor tells the IRS he now acts for the estate by filing:",
 "Form 56", ["Form 1310", "Form 2848", "Form 4810"],
 "Form 56, Notice Concerning Fiduciary Relationship, notifies the IRS of a fiduciary relationship. The fiduciary may then appoint a representative on Form 2848."),
("An unenrolled preparer with an AFSP Record of Completion prepared and signed a client's return. He may represent her before:",
 "A revenue agent", ["An appeals officer", "A revenue officer", "IRS Chief Counsel"],
 "Unenrolled preparers with the required AFSP records may represent only before revenue agents, customer service representatives and similar employees during an examination of a return they prepared."),
("An unenrolled preparer lacks a current AFSP record for the year he prepared a client's return. He may:",
 "View data under Form 8821", ["Represent her in the audit", "Sign a waiver for her", "Handle her Appeals case"],
 "Without the AFSP records the Form 2848 instructions require, an unenrolled preparer cannot represent. The client may still let him inspect or receive her tax information by filing Form 8821."),
("A client's Form 2848 covers only her Form 1040. The IRS proposes a trust fund recovery penalty against her. The EA:",
 "Needs a line 3 entry for it", ["Is covered automatically", "Is covered for 60 days", "Is covered as a related penalty"],
 "The instructions' example says a power of attorney for a Form 1040 does not cover a trust fund recovery penalty. A civil penalty not tied to the listed return must be described on line 3."),
("For an EA to sign Form 8857 for a client, line 3 of the Form 2848 must:",
 "Name innocent spouse relief", ["List every joint tax year", "Name both spouses on it", "Have the line 4 box checked"],
 "The instructions let the representative sign Form 8857 only if line 3 describes innocent spouse relief. Otherwise the taxpayer must sign Form 8857 personally."),
("To pull a client's transcripts through a private intermediate service provider, the representative needs:",
 "A line 5a check for that use", ["A line 4 check for that use", "A line 6 box for that use", "A line 3 entry for that use"],
 "A representative may not use an intermediate service provider to retrieve tax information unless the taxpayer checks that box on line 5a. Without it, the e-Services Transcript Delivery System is used."),
("A client's address on Form 2848 is newer than the IRS's records. To change her last known address she files:",
 "Form 8822", ["Form 8821", "A new Form 2848", "Form 56"],
 "Address information on Form 2848 does not change the taxpayer's last known address. Form 8822 changes a home address and Form 8822-B a business address."),
("An EA moves her office. For her clients' existing Forms 2848, she:",
 "Sends a signed notice", ["Files new Forms 2848", "Updates her PTIN only", "Waits for the CAF update"],
 "The IRS does not require a new Form 2848 when a representative's address changes. A written notice with the new information and her signature, sent where the forms were filed, is enough."),
("A client gives a durable power of attorney instead of Form 2848. To have it recorded on the CAF, the representative:",
 "Attaches a Form 2848", ["Files it with Form 8821", "Records it through e-Services", "Mails it to the CAF unit alone"],
 "A non-IRS power of attorney meeting 26 CFR 601.503(a) is accepted, but it cannot be recorded on the CAF unless a completed Form 2848 is attached, signed by the representative."),
("A client signs Form 2848 with an electronic signature. The form must be submitted:",
 "Online only", ["By fax only", "By mail only", "In person at an office"],
 "The instructions say a Form 2848 with an electronic signature, or a digitized image of a handwritten one, may only be submitted online at IRS.gov/Submit2848."),
("Without a line 5a grant, can a representative let the IRS disclose the client's return to her lender?",
 "No, only with a line 5a grant", ["Yes, it is default authority", "Yes, if the lender asks for it", "Only by phone with the IRS"],
 "A representative cannot execute consents allowing the IRS to disclose return information to a third party unless the taxpayer specifically delegates that authority on line 5a."),
("A taxpayer's brother, who is not a practitioner, may represent her before the IRS:",
 "With proof of his authority", ["Only with his own PTIN", "Only in her presence", "Only after filing Form 56"],
 "Section 10.7(c)(1)(i) lets an individual represent a member of his immediate family, even if the taxpayer is absent, on presenting identification and proof of authority."),
("For a partnership under the centralized audit regime, the partnership representative is designated:",
 "On its tax return", ["On a Form 2848 filing", "On a Form 8821 filing", "On a Form 56 notice"],
 "The instructions say Form 2848 is not used to designate a partnership representative. The designation is made on the partnership return for the year, and Form 2848 lets the representative appoint an agent."),
]
